    thinking: "**Defining the Scope**\n\nI\'ve initiated an in-depth analysis of the user\'s initial request. I\'m focusing on the implied roles, specified objective, key guidelines, and the critical output format. My primary task is to interpret this and ensure a clear understanding before proceeding with further processing.\n\n\n**Analyzing the User Intent**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the user\'s apparent goal. It seems they want me to process text, specifically meeting transcripts, into Markdown tables and specific sections, even though I\'m in a coding environment. This is a crucial pivot. I\'ve re-evaluated the \"unexpected error\" messages; it looks like the platform may have triggered them, which makes this task even more peculiar.\n\n\n**Formulating the Application**\n\nI\'m now shifting gears. The initial persona prompt is suggestive. Instead of directly adopting the persona, it seems the user intends for me to *build an application* to embody this role. I\'m moving toward creating a React app that accepts meeting transcripts, leverages the Gemini API with the provided system prompt, and outputs formatted meeting minutes. This aligns with the platform\'s app-building capabilities. My next step will be to thoroughly plan out this application.\n\n\n**Designing the UI**\n\nI\'m now deep in UI design, envisioning the components. I\'ve settled on a clear layout: a header, a textarea for input, a generation button, and a markdown output display. A loading spinner will handle the processing. I have picked the Gemini-3-flash-preview model. Dependencies like react-markdown and remark-gfm are also required.\n\n\n**Implementing the App**\n\nI\'m now in the thick of implementation. I\'m building out `src/App.tsx`, which will handle the core UI and the API calls to the Gemini model. I\'m focusing on the component that renders the markdown and getting the API integration to function correctly. I\'ve drafted some basic TypeScript for the core components, setting up state for the transcript, the output, and a loading indicator. I\'m also planning to use `react-markdown` and `remark-gfm` for safe markdown rendering, and I\'m currently setting up the Google GenAI object using the user\'s key.\n\n\n**Debugging the Logic**\n\nI\'m now focusing on integrating the Gemini API and handling potential errors. I\'ve written an `onSubmit` function that sends the transcript to the model. I\'ve also incorporated error handling for potential API failures, to display a user-friendly message. I\'m leveraging `react-markdown` and `remark-gfm` to ensure safe markdown rendering. My next step is compiling the applet.\n\n```javascript\nimport React, { useState } from \'react\';\nimport ReactMarkdown from \'react-markdown\';\nimport remarkGfm from \'remark-gfm\';\n\nfunction App() {\n  const [transcript, setTranscript] = useState(\'\');\n  const [result, setResult] = useState(\'\');\n  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(false);\n\n  const onSubmit = async () => {\n    if (!transcript.trim()) return;\n    setLoading(true);\n    try {\n      const response = await ai.models.generateContent({\n        model: \'gemini-3-flash-preview\',\n        contents: transcript,\n        config: {\n          systemInstruction: SYSTEM_PROMPT,\n        }\n      });\n      setResult(response.text || \'\');\n    } catch (e) {\n      console.error(e);\n      setResult(\'\347\231\274\347\224\237\351\214\257\350\252\244\357\274\214\350\253\213\347\250\215\345\276\214\345\206\215\350\251\246\343\200\202\');\n    } finally {\n      setLoading(false);\n    }\n  };\n\n  // ... render UI ...\n}\n```\n\n\n**Embedding the Prompt**\n\nI\'ve integrated the user\'s detailed instructions into the system instruction for the Gemini API call. This will ensure the model adheres strictly to the desired role, objective, guidelines, and output format when generating the meeting minutes. This is a critical step to get the app running.\n\n\n**Refining the Output**\n\nI\'m now integrating the user\'s latest output format specifications. I\'m focusing on the Markdown structure and the table formats, particularly the \"\346\234\203\350\255\260\345\237\272\346\234\254\350\263\207\350\250\212\" section and the structure of the \"\346\234\203\350\255\260\351\207\215\351\273\236\346\221\230\350\246\201\" section. I\'ll need to adapt the API call to ensure the AI\'s response adheres to this meticulous structure. I\'m prioritizing accuracy for the AI\'s output, and the quality of the markdown output.\n\n\n**Structuring the Output**\n\nI\'m now integrating the provided \"Discussion & Resolutions,\" \"Key Meeting Points,\" and \"Action Item Tracking List\" structures into my output formatting. I\'m focusing on ensuring the AI generates the required sections in the correct Markdown format. This requires careful parsing and the generation of formatted tables and bullet points. I\'m prioritizing adherence to all formatting rules.\n\n\n"
