    thinking: "**Constructing the UI Components**\n\nI\'m now focused on building the user interface in `src/App.tsx`. The core components are taking shape: a prominent title (\"\351\253\230\351\232\216\345\260\210\346\241\210\347\247\230\346\233\270 - \346\234\203\350\255\260\347\264\200\351\214\204\347\224\237\346\210\220\345\231\250\"), a sizeable textarea for transcript input, a \"Generate Minutes\" button, and a dedicated Markdown rendering area. Initial structure is complete, time for styling.\n\n\n**Refining the App\'s Metadata**\n\nI\'ve just added the application\'s metadata, including the display name. I\'m actively working on `src/App.tsx`, and I\'ve started defining its core structure. I\'m focusing on key UI elements: a prominent title, a text area for transcript input, a generation button, and a markdown rendering area. Basic structure is ready; time to get it pretty!\n\n\n**Defining the Output Format**\n\nI\'m now completely focused on defining the output format, ensuring it aligns with a professional business tone. The structure is being meticulously followed: from the basic meeting information to the key takeaways section with detailed tables. I\'m focusing on accurately capturing all necessary components in the output format. I will soon be ready to move to extracting the necessary content.\n\n\n**Structuring the Meeting Notes**\n\nI\'m now deep in defining the structure for the meeting minutes, mapping out sections for background, objectives, discussions, resolutions, key takeaways, and an actionable item tracking list. I\'m focusing on incorporating distinct sections for topics and the structured elements within, such as decision-making, consensus, and action item specifications. I\'ll make sure to integrate the critical information into a clear, usable format.\n\n\n**Formulating the Observations**\n\nI\'m now formulating \"Secretary\'s Observations & Suggestions,\" considering Management Observations and Potential Risks. I\'m focusing on providing insights to improve management or inter-departmental collaboration, and highlighting potential risks with suggestions.\n\n\n**Handling Error Scenarios**\n\nI\'m now implementing error handling and user feedback mechanisms. When the generation process fails, I\'ll display a user-friendly error message, specifically addressing network issues or suggesting a retry. I also added a \"Copy to Clipboard\" button that provides feedback after a successful copy. I\'m focusing on user experience, and making sure that all edge cases are considered.\n\n\n**Designing the Input Section**\n\nI\'m now integrating the transcript input section into the UI. I\'ve built a multi-line text area, complete with placeholder text to guide the user. I\'ve also added explanatory text below the title. This includes text to prompt the user to input either their transcript or notes. I\'ve set up the necessary state management for user input and disabled the \"Generate\" button when loading or if there\'s no input.\n\n\n**Implementing the \"Generate\" Button**\n\nI\'ve just refined the \"Generate Minutes\" button\'s functionality within `src/App.tsx`. I\'ve integrated loading state management, ensuring it visually represents the processing period. Now, the button displays a loading spinner and \"\346\255\243\345\234\250\346\217\220\347\205\211\346\234\203\350\255\260\347\264\200\351\214\204...\" during generation, switching back to \"\347\224\237\346\210\220\345\260\210\346\245\255\346\234\203\350\255\260\347\264\200\351\214\204\" with a send icon on completion. The design is clean and I\'m keen on enhancing the user experience.\n\n\n**Refining the Output Display**\n\nI\'m now integrating a \"Copy to Clipboard\" button alongside the rendered output. It will offer visual feedback and change its label to \"\345\267\262\350\244\207\350\243\275\" (Copied) upon clicking, using a checkmark icon to signify the successful copy, and it will be visible only when there\'s an actual output to copy. I\'m focusing on user convenience and visual clarity.\n\n\n"
