  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Clarifying Transcription Goals**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the core request: real-time transcription. The user is aiming for this as a function within the app itself. The initial prompt clarified my role, now this defines what the app should do. Real-time transcription is a key ingredient!\n\n\n**Defining Segmentation Strategy**\n\nI\'m now thinking about how to handle the segmentation requirement, given the choice of the Web Speech API. I\'m considering accumulating the transcript from the API. We can trigger a partial analysis, maybe every 5 minutes or every X characters. Or, we could give the user control to start and stop analysis.\n\n\n**Evaluating Chunking Approaches**\n\nI\'m now comparing chunking strategies for Gemini interaction. Approach 1 involves pre-defined intervals for sending text for key point extraction, followed by merging the results. Approach 2 leans into providing the user more immediate control and triggering on their action. The prompt supports chunking as a key requirement. I\'m focusing on user control.\n\n\n**Refining Segmentation Logic**\n\nI\'m now iterating on the segmentation approach for the live transcript. I\'ve decided to maintain an array of transcript chunks as the transcript comes in, which can be useful when generating the report. I\'m focusing on user control and \"live analysis\" during recording. Each time a text chunk reaches a certain length, I\'ll send it to Gemini for key point extraction. This aligns with the user\'s \"\345\210\206\346\256\265\351\200\262\350\241\214\345\210\206\346\236\220\" request, offering intermediate summaries.\n\n\n**Outlining Interface Requirements**\n\nI\'m now concretely defining the user interface elements and system interactions. A clear \"Microphone\" button for starting and stopping is essential, alongside a real-time transcript display. I plan to use the Web Speech API and have determined the need to handle events such as `onresult` and `onend`, including continuous listening. I\'ve also solidified a strategy for handling analysis of the user\'s transcript via an intermediate \"Partial Summary.\"\n\n\n**Implementing Microphone Access**\n\nI\'m now integrating microphone permissions into the system. I have updated the `metadata.json` file to include `\"microphone\"` within `requestFramePermissions`. I\'m starting to draft the core code and am beginning to build the app state with essential variables. The inclusion of the SpeechRecognition setup with a focus on traditional Chinese is a current area of focus. My priorities are to build the `isRecording`, `transcript`, `interimTranscript`, `segments`, and `finalReport` variables to prepare the application for real-time transcription and analysis.\n\n\n**Refining Summarization Triggers**\n\nI\'m now iterating on when to trigger the summarization. I\'ve switched from waiting until \"Generate Final Report\" to a more dynamic approach. I\'ll automatically analyze chunks of the transcript as it comes in. I\'ll maintain `analyzedTextLength` and when `transcript.length - analyzedTextLength` exceeds 1000 characters, I\'ll slice and send that to Gemini. This keeps the summarization live and addresses the user\'s need for \"\345\210\206\346\256\265\351\200\262\350\241\214\345\210\206\346\236\220.\" I\'m prioritizing the user\'s experience.\n\n\n**Designing UI Interactions**\n\nI\'m now focusing on UI refinements, particularly for segmented analysis. I\'m visualizing the UI, with a clear split: a left panel for recording and live transcript, and a right panel with tabs for \"\345\215\263\346\231\202\345\210\206\346\256\265\346\221\230\350\246\201\" and \"\346\234\200\347\265\202\346\234\203\350\255\260\347\264\200\351\214\204.\" The \"Live Segment Summaries\" tab will update with analyses as they\'re generated, and the \"Final Meeting Minutes\" tab will be triggered by a \"Generate Final Minutes\" button, which feeds the existing segment summaries to Gemini for a final, structured report, priorit