  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Audio Alternatives**\n\nI\'m currently dealing with recurring FFmpeg loading issues when handling substantial audio files, specifically around 300MB. I am actively seeking alternative methods to split the audio into smaller segments suitable for speech processing.\n\n\n**Evaluating Audio Strategies**\n\nI\'ve been evaluating several methods to split large audio files without relying on FFmpeg, considering browser limitations. I\'m prioritizing options that avoid external WASM dependencies. The `AudioContext` method seems promising; it allows decoding the audio and slicing the `AudioBuffer` directly within the browser. While it carries a risk of memory strain for a 300MB file, it\'s often feasible on desktop browsers, making it the most robust fallback. Blob slicing is an option, but works only for raw, uncompressed files.\n\n\n**Implementing Web Audio Fallback**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `processFileWithWebAudio` function. It will serve as a fallback when FFmpeg is unavailable or fails with large files. I\'m focusing on handling audio decoding via `AudioContext` and segmenting the decoded audio. The `handleFileUpload` function will be updated to utilize this fallback. I will add UI updates to indicate the fallback is being used. However, I\'ve realized that decoding a compressed large file fully into an `AudioBuffer` may cause a large memory footprint.\n\n**Exploring MediaRecorder Fallback**\n\nConsidering the memory constraints, using the `MediaRecorder` API seems like a better approach for splitting without FFmpeg. This avoids a full in-memory decoding. The goal is to make it easy to process the file in smaller chunks.\n\n\n"
