  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Memory Limits**\n\nI\'ve determined that the current approach with `audioBufferToWav` and `decodeAudioData` is unsustainable for the large 300MB file. Holding the entire raw PCM data (potentially exceeding 2GB) in memory poses an immediate problem. These functions will inevitably fail due to browser memory constraints when processing this file size.\n\n\n**Implementing Chunking Strategy**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a chunking strategy to avoid memory limits and network timeouts. My initial plan involved 15MB chunks, but I\'ve realized that naive slicing of MP3 files could create invalid audio segments. Although modern decoders are often resilient, this is not guaranteed, and may cause errors. For WAV, it\'s easier, as I can just add a header to each slice. The final chunk size should ensure minimal data loss.\n\n\n**Refining Slice Handling**\n\nI\'ve decided to refine the chunking strategy. I can accept negligible frame loss at chunk boundaries. My current focus is to refine the `processFileBySlicing` function. It\'ll be triggered if FFmpeg fails with a large file. The approach involves slicing into ~15MB chunks and sending each as a UI `Chunk`. I\'ll also add a button to \"Skip FFmpeg\" or \"Use Compatibility Mode\" more prominently. Furthermore, I\'ll update the UI to show a \"Manual Slicing Mode\" option if the user desires. I also need to make sure the users browser supports `AudioContext`\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "mez8uxlg"
      name: "multi_edit_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"Instruction\":\"Implement Blob Slicing as a fallback for large files when FFmpeg fails.\",\"ReplacementChunks\":[{\"ReplacementContent\":\"        if (ffmpegLoadedRef.current) {\\n          await processFileWithFFmpeg(file, statusChunkId);\\n        } else {\\n          // Fallback for large files when FFmpeg fails\\n          if (file.size > 20 * 1024 * 1024) {\\n            await processFileBySlicing(file, statusChunkId);\\n          } else {\\n            await processFileLegacy(file, statusChunkId);\\n          }\\n        }\",\"TargetContent\":\"        if (ffmpegLoadedRef.current) {\\n          await processFileWithFFmpeg(file, statusChunkId);\\n        } else {\\n          if (file.size > 30 * 1024 * 1024) {\\n            throw new Error(\'\346\252\224\346\241\210\351\201\216\345\244\247\344\270\224\350\231\225\347\220\206\347\265\204\344\273\266\350\274\211\345\205\245\345\244\261\346\225\227\343\200\202\350\253\213\346\252\242\346\237\245\347\266\262\350\267\257\351\200\243\347\267\232\344\270\246\351\207\215\346\226\260\346\225\264\347\220\206\351\240\201\351\235\242\343\200\202\');\\n          }\\n          await processFileLegacy(file, statusChunkId);\\n        }\"},{\"ReplacementContent\":\"  const processFileBySlicing = async (file: File, statusChunkId: number) => {\\n    const CHUNK_SIZE = 15 * 1024 * 1024; // 15MB chunks\\n    const totalChunks = Math.ceil(file.size / CHUNK_SIZE);\\n    \\n    setChunks(prev => prev.map(c => c.id === statusChunkId ? { ...c, text: `\347\265\204\344\273\266\350\274\211\345\205\245\345\244\261\346\225\227\357\274\214\345\210\207\346\217\233\350\207\263\343\200\214\347\233\270\345\256\271\345\210\207\347\211\207\346\250\241\345\274\217\343\200\215\350\231\225\347\220\206\344\270\255 (${file.name})...` } : c));\\n    \\n    setChunks(prev => prev.filter(c => c.id !== statusChunkId));\\n\\n    for (let i = 0; i < totalChunks; i++) {\\n      const start = i * CHUNK_SIZE;\\n      const end = Math.min(start + CHUNK_SIZE, file.size);\\n      const blob = file.slice(start, end);\\n      const base64Data = await fileToBase64(blob);\\n\\n      const segmentChunk: Chunk = {\\n        id: Date.now() + i,\\n        text: `\351\214\204\351\237\263\345\210\206\346\256\265 ${i + 1}/${totalChunks} (\347\233\270\345\256\271\346\250\241\345\274\217 - \347\264\204\347\254\254 ${i * 5} \345\210\206\351\220\230\350\265\267)`,\\n        isAnalyzing: true,\\n        audio: { fileName: `${file.name} (Part ${i + 1})`, mimeType: file.type || \'audio/mpeg\', data: base64Data }\\n      };\\n\\n      setChunks(prev => [...prev, segmentChunk]);\\n      analyzeChunk(segmentChunk);\\n      \\n      // Small delay to prevent UI freeze\\n      await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 500));\\n    }\\n  };\\n\\n  const processFileLegacy = async (file: File, statusChunkId: number) => {\",\"TargetContent\":\"  const processFileLegacy = async (file: File, statusChunkId: number) => {\"}],\"TargetFile\":\"/src/App.tsx\",\"toolSummary\":\"Implement Blob Slicing fallback for large files when FFmpeg fails.\"}"
      thought_signature: ""
