ror message likely masks the true cause.\n\n\n**Refining Chunk Size & MimeType**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on data size issues. Even at a 15MB slice, base64 encoding might hit the 20MB `inlineData` limit. Reducing the chunk size to 10MB is my next step for safety. Also, I\'m verifying the `mimeType` in `processFileBySlicing` and the `analyzeChunk` function. I am checking if `file.type` defaults to \'audio/mpeg\'.\n\nI\'ve also just identified a critical bug in `analyzeChunk`. The Gemini API expects an array of content objects, but I passed a slightly incorrect format with extra brackets around the part. I\'ll correct this formatting in the next iteration.\n\n\n**Improving Error Handling**\n\nI\'m now investigating my current error handling, and making adjustments based on recent observations. My `contents` format seems correct based on example code. I\'m checking to make sure that the API key is initialized correctly, and also ensuring the system handles potential API failures gracefully. I need to improve error detection and logging.\n\n\n"
