  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Potential Causes**\n\nI\'ve homed in on two primary suspects for the issue. The user is likely encountering the `processFileBySlicing` fallback either because FFmpeg is taking an extended time to initialize, or perhaps `useCompatibilityMode` has been activated. Additionally, the \"no audio stream\" error seems directly tied to the raw byte slicing method. I will begin by fixing `processFileWithFFmpeg`.\n\n\n**Refining FFmpeg Approach**\n\nI\'ve decided to refine the `processFileWithFFmpeg` function. I\'m updating the FFmpeg command to re-encode to MP3 with `libmp3lame` at 128k bitrate. This guarantees a valid audio stream, which should fix the \"no audio stream\" error. I am also renaming the current slicing method.\n\n\n**Improving Fallback Strategy**\n\nI\'m now revisiting the fallback strategy, specifically for large files and the limitations of FFmpeg. I\'m considering the `Web Audio API` as a possible alternative. I\'ve realized raw slicing might work *sometimes* for MP3s if they are aligned with frame boundaries, but it is unreliable, and fails for M4A. I\'ll update `processFileWithFFmpeg` to re-encode and I\'ll also check for `.m4a` file uploads.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "4fxlphb1"
      name: "multi_edit_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"Instruction\":\"Fix the \\\"no audio stream\\\" error by re-encoding segments to MP3 in FFmpeg and improving the slicing fallback.\",\"ReplacementChunks\":[{\"ReplacementContent\":\"    // Slice into 10-minute segments and re-encode to MP3 for maximum compatibility\\n    // Re-encoding ensures that each segment is a valid standalone MP3 file\\n    const outputExt = \'.mp3\'; \\n    await ffmpeg.exec([\\n      \'-i\', inputName, \\n      \'-f\', \'segment\', \\n      \'-segment_time\', \'600\', \\n      \'-c:a\', \'libmp3lame\', \\n      \'-b:a\', \'64k\', // 64k is enough for voice and keeps file size small\\n      `out%03d${outputExt}`\\n    ]);\",\"TargetContent\":\"    // Slice into 10-minute segments without re-encoding (very fast)\\n    // We use .mp3 as output for better compatibility if possible, or keep original extension\\n    const outputExt = \'.mp3\'; \\n    await ffmpeg.exec([\'-i\', inputName, \'-f\', \'segment\', \'-segment_time\', \'600\', \'-c\', \'copy\', `out%03d${outputExt}`]);\"},{\"ReplacementContent\":\"  const processFileBySlicing = async (file: File, statusChunkId: number) => {\\n    // WARNING: Raw byte slicing is unreliable for compressed audio.\\n    // We only use this as a last resort if FFmpeg fails to load.\\n    const CHUNK_SIZE = 10 * 1024 * 1024; // 10MB chunks\\n    const totalChunks = Math.ceil(file.size / CHUNK_SIZE);\\n    \\n    setChunks(prev => prev.map(c => c.id === statusChunkId ? { ...c, text: `\346\255\243\345\234\250\344\273\245\343\200\214\347\267\212\346\200\245\347\233\270\345\256\271\346\250\241\345\274\217\343\200\215\350\231\225\347\220\206\344\270\255 (${file.name})... \346\263\250\346\204\217\357\274\232\346\255\244\346\250\241\345\274\217\345\217\257\350\203\275\345\233\240\351\237\263\350\250\212\346\240\274\345\274\217\344\270\215\347\233\270\345\256\271\350\200\214\345\244\261\346\225\227\343\200\202` } : c));\\n\\n    for (let i = 0; i < totalChunks; i++) {\\n      const start = i 