  user_input {
    user_response: "We are still getting the Gemini API error: \"INVALID_ARGUMENT: The input file does not have an audio stream\". This means the audio Blob being created by MediaRecorder and passed to the API (or FFmpeg if used) is either empty, not finalized correctly, or in a format Gemini does not accept. Please completely rewrite the MediaRecorder logic to ensure recordings are created using type: \'audio/webm\' (or the most compatible MIME type), and ensure that when chunks are sent to the Gemini API, they contain valid audio data. If using FFmpeg to slice, ensure you are properly waiting for the process to finish and reading the output correctly. Consider switching to simpler slicing or just sending the whole Blob if it is short enough."
    items {
      text: "We are still getting the Gemini API error: \"INVALID_ARGUMENT: The input file does not have an audio stream\". This means the audio Blob being created by MediaRecorder and passed to the API (or FFmpeg if used) is either empty, not finalized correctly, or in a format Gemini does not accept. Please completely rewrite the MediaRecorder logic to ensure recordings are created using type: \'audio/webm\' (or the most compatible MIME type), and ensure that when chunks are sent to the Gemini API, they contain valid audio data. If using FFmpeg to slice, ensure you are properly waiting for the process to finish and reading the output correctly. Consider switching to simpler slicing or just sending the whole Blob if it is short enough."
    }
  }
