    thinking: "**Refining FFmpeg Integration**\n\nI\'m now focusing on improving `processFileWithFFmpeg`. My priority is ensuring correct process waiting and proper output handling, as the user advised. I\'ll make sure FFmpeg processes are waited for, and output is captured appropriately in the implementation. I\'m taking the feedback seriously, ensuring robust integration of FFmpeg within the code.\n\n\n**Sequencing File Operations**\n\nI realized `ffmpeg.exec` is asynchronous but might return before files are fully written. To address this, I\'ve implemented a check using `ffmpeg.listDir(\'.\')` to verify file existence and sort the output files to guarantee processing order using `.sort((a, b) => a.name.localeCompare(b.name))`. This is designed to ensure that `analyzeChunk` processes these files in the correct sequence.\n\n\n**Confirming Model Usage**\n\nI\'ve re-examined the code and confirmed that `analyzeChunk` is indeed using `gemini-2.0-flash`, as requested. I\'ve also verified that the `processFileDirectly` function correctly handles the file and its associated MIME type. My focus is now on ensuring this function correctly processes incoming WebM files and passes the correct data to `analyzeChunk`, which now seems to be working as expected.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "ut1fslfb"
      name: "edit_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"Instruction\":\"Sort output files in FFmpeg processing to ensure correct order and add more logging.\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"    const files = await ffmpeg.listDir(\'.\');\\n    const outputFiles = files\\n      .filter(f => f.name.startsWith(\'out\') && !f.isDir)\\n      .sort((a, b) => a.name.localeCompare(b.name));\\n    \\n    console.log(`FFmpeg slicing complete. Found ${outputFiles.length} segments.`);\\n    setChunks(prev => prev.filter(c => c.id !== statusChunkId));\\n\\n    for (let i = 0; i < outputFiles.length; i++) {\\n      const fileName = outputFiles[i].name;\\n      console.log(`Reading segment: ${fileName}`);\\n      const data = await ffmpeg.readFile(fileName);\\n      const blob = new Blob([data], { type: \'audio/mpeg\' });\\n      const base64Data = await fileToBase64(blob);\\n\\n      const segmentChunk: Chunk = {\\n        id: Date.now() + i,\\n        text: `\351\214\204\351\237\263\345\210\206\346\256\265 ${i + 1}/${outputFiles.length} (\347\264\204\347\254\254 ${i * 10} \345\210\206\351\220\230\350\265\267)`,\\n        isAnalyzing: true,\\n        audio: { fileName: `${file.name} (Part ${i + 1})`, mimeType: \'audio/mpeg\', data: base64Data }\\n      };\\n\\n      setChunks(prev => [...prev, segmentChunk]);\\n      await analyzeChunk(segmentChunk); // Process sequentially to avoid rate limits\\n      await ffmpeg.deleteFile(fileName);\\n    }\",\"TargetContent\":\"    const files = await ffmpeg.listDir(\'.\');\\n    const outputFiles = files.filter(f => f.name.startsWith(\'out\') && !f.isDir);\\n    \\n    setChunks(prev => prev.filter(c => c.id !== statusChunkId));\\n\\n    for (let i = 0; i < outputFiles.length; i++) {\\n      const fileName = outputFiles[i].name;\\n      const data = await ffmpeg.readFile(fileName);\\n      const blob = new Blob([data], { type: \'audio/mpeg\' });\\n      const base64Data = await fileToBase64(blob);\\n\\n      const segmentChunk: Chunk = {\\n        id: Date.now() + i,\\n        text: `\351\214\204\351\237\263\345\210\206\346\256\265 ${i + 1}/${outputFiles.length} (\347\264\204\347\254\254 ${i * 10} \345\210\206\351\220\230\350\265\267)`,\\n        isAnalyzing: true,\\n        audio: { fileName: `${file.name} (Part ${i + 1})`, mimeType: \'audio/mpeg\', data: base64Data }\\n      };\\n\\n      setChunks(prev => [...prev, segmentChunk]);\\n      analyzeChunk(segmentChunk);\\n      await ffmpeg.deleteFile(fileName);\\n    }\",\"TargetFile\":\"/src/App.tsx\",\"toolSummary\":\"Improve FFmpeg segment processing with sorting and sequential analysis.\"}"
