  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Investigating Audio Uploads**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the audio file upload issue, and am primarily reviewing the `handleFileUpload` function and the associated audio decoding and slicing processes. I believe I need to understand why the browser crashes/freezes when an audio file upload is attempted. I\'m hoping to identify the root cause of this behavior.\n\n\n**Analyzing Potential Bottlenecks**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on potential performance bottlenecks. The synchronous nature of `processFileBySlicing` is under scrutiny, particularly the chunking logic. Although the `async` while loop seemed safe initially, its potential to block or not update correctly is still under consideration. My focus is now on ensuring asynchronous chunking and memory-efficient operations to eliminate UI freezes. I\'ll be investigating the detailed steps involved in `processFileBySlicing` function.\n\n\n**Simplifying Chunking Logic**\n\nI\'m now simplifying the chunking logic to avoid excessive memory consumption during audio file processing. I\'m focusing on alternatives to `audioCtx.decodeAudioData` when dealing with potentially large audio files. It seems the initial decoding, especially with large files, might be the source of the crashes. My current task is to refine the chunking implementation to be more memory-efficient and avoid crashing the browser. I am hoping to avoid the use of `audioCtx.decodeAudioData` completely.\n\n\n**Refining Async Audio Handling**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the synchronous loop within `audioBufferToWav`. This loop\'s iterations through a potentially massive audio buffer are causing the UI to freeze. To resolve this, I\'m focusing on simplifying `handleFileUpload` and making `processFileBySlicing` less memory-intensive, potentially by making it more asynchronous. I\'m also planning to rely on FFmpeg for slicing, as that is the safest approach.\n\n\n**Improving File Handling**\n\nI\'m now focusing on directly addressing the synchronous operations. Specifically, I plan to eliminate the `while` loop within `handleFileUpload`. The synchronous `for` loop in `audioBufferToWav` is also a priority; I\'ll optimize it or make it chunk-based with `setTimeout`. Ideally, FFmpeg will handle slicing, but if it\'s unavailable, I\'ll refactor `processFileBySlicing` to avoid that troublesome `for` loop, or at least break it up. I will also refactor `handleFileUpload` to ensure it is more streamlined.\n\n\n**Prioritizing FFmpeg Utilization**\n\nI\'m now completely removing the risky `processFileBySlicing` and `audioBufferToWav` functions; they were indeed memory bombs. My focus is now ensuring FFmpeg is used wherever possible. I\'ve updated `handleFileUpload` to prioritize FFmpeg, and will implement better error handling with promises and state management for those times when FFmpeg is not available, avoiding large file decoding on the client-side altogether. I will now integrate an FFmpeg chunking implementation.\n\n\n"
