  checkpoint {
    user_intent: "Improve FFmpeg Loading and Fallback Logic\nThe user wants to improve the FFmpeg loading process by increasing the timeout duration and implementing a fallback mechanism. If FFmpeg fails to load after the extended timeout, the application should allow direct upload of the original file to Gemini, bypassing the slicing process. This ensures that the application remains functional even when FFmpeg is unavailable or times out."
    intent_only: true
    included_step_index_end: 50
    conversation_log_uris: "file:///.gemini/antigravity/brain/ce67f19d-a4c5-4b10-bcd6-71c0a3db9c78/.system_generated/logs/overview.txt"
    user_requests: "Uploading an audio file causes the browser to crash or freeze in an infinite loop. Please completely review `handleFileUpload` and your audio decoding/slicing functions. Remove any `while` loops or synchronous recursive functions that could be causing an infinite loop. Ensure that when you chunk the audio, you are doing it asynchronously (e.g., using `setTimeout` or Web Workers if necessary, or just avoid complex memory-heavy operations on the main thread). Simplify the logic: just read the audio file and send it to Gemini in reasonable chunks without doing heavy byte-level manipulation that freezes the UI. Apply the fix and simplify."
    user_requests: "FFmpeg loading is timing out in this environment. Please update the loadFFmpeg function: 1. Increase timeout to 120000ms. 2. If all CDNs fail, set a flag or allow the handleFileUpload function to proceed with the original file instead of slicing, so we can still try to upload directly to Gemini. 3. Ensure the direct upload path to Gemini is functional even if FFmpeg is missing."
    user_requests: "FFmpeg loading is timing out in this environment. Please update the loadFFmpeg function: 1. Increase timeout to 120000ms. 2. If all CDNs fail, set a flag or allow the handleFileUpload function to proceed with the original file instead of slicing, so we can still try to upload directly to Gemini. 3. Ensure the direct upload path to Gemini is functional even if FFmpeg is missing."
  }
}
